{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1524235-the-invictus-has-a-lot-of-titles-for-so-few-people","id":1524235,"title":"The Invictus has a LOT of titles for so few people","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-10-18T13:15:26-07:00","id":1524235,"title":"The Invictus has a LOT of titles for so few people","content":"I was reading the 1st Edition Invictus book and it struck me as odd that the Invictus have whopping 27 separate Titles of Function listed and 8 Titles of Tribute. The go-to number of vampire populations I've found is between 1-in-50.000 to 1-in-100.000. Without even accounting for the other Covenants, by that metric there's a mere handful of cities in the US that would have more vampires in it than the Invictus have individual titles to hand out.<br /> <br /> And since in Requiem the vampire organizations are supposed to be more decentralized and city specific, it just feels odd that the Invictus are written up as this expansive aristocratic group of duties and intrigue and deeply ritualized social conduct, when 99% of places couldn't fill out a fraction of it possible ranks, even if every Invictus pulled double-duty. <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24240-tungul","name":"Tungul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-18T13:54:49-07:00","id":1524239,"title":"","content":"From reading the preamble, to me it's pretty clear that not every city is expected to have every title of function. The point is to give every Invictus member their own unique position, so you only need as many positions as you have members.<br /> <br /> The titles of tribute are based on members having actually earned those titles. If none of your characters have conquered the city, then none of them get to be dukes or duchesses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-18T14:40:41-07:00","id":1524241,"title":"","content":"While Michael has the right of it I also want to point out that 1:100,000 you see isn't 1 vampire per 100,000 people in the city, it is worldwide population, and honestly, never actually obeyed.<br /> <br /> Take New Orleans for example, it has a population of less than 400,000 but it has dozens of vampire residents and sometimes far more vampires visiting, I think the book said it can get up to 50 or so visiting vampires.<br /> <br /> ETA: I found the actual figure of visiting kindred for New Orleans. The city averages 40 visiting kindred per night. So by visiting kindred alone it has 10x the recommended kindred population.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","user":"ShadowcatX","date":". 10-18-2023, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-18T16:26:33-07:00","id":1524245,"title":"","content":"True we never followed the population ratio in our games and went with having a few dozen Kindred in our nearest big city that has just slightly over 1.2 million people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-18T20:24:50-07:00","id":1524255,"title":"","content":"I generally make an argument to keep to canon as much as possible, but when it comes to population numbers and ratios, even other writers and devs have come around to saying &quot;Yeah, just ignore that&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T05:56:56-07:00","id":1524270,"title":"","content":"I personally try to avoid to fill out a city with several dozens of kindred. I'd like to avoid &quot;blade&quot; style where vampires are no more than cannon fodder. I'd rather prefer to have few &quot;resident&quot; vampires (which are well characterized and relevant, perhaps adding a few ghouls (with also high power) or nomad to results in an interesting environment that does not let the character feel &quot;lonley&quot;. For this I think that WoD population ratio fit the bill. A big city still may have up to 30-40 kindred, which are more than enough to give a strong political set up also for Invictus.<br /> About the invictus titles, not all titles must be covered in a city. There might be high title which are based elsewhere and are like a boogieman appearing only in dramatic instances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7079,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","user":"Marcus","date":". 10-19-2023, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7079-marcus","name":"Marcus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7079_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-19T09:28:12-07:00","id":1524281,"title":"","content":"I'd go with having a certain number of covenants in a city that have a strong presence such as Invictus, Carthians or Ordo Dracul and tend have the others with little to no standing in our city.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T14:40:41-07:00","id":1541601,"title":"","content":"Also the limits of vampires per humans is a limit for *active* vampires. I always imagined the Invictus to have far more torpid vampires than any other covenants, so the titles could be occupied by torpid monsters, buried deep beneath a skyscrapper or any other stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26829-vumerion","name":"Vumerion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T14:43:44-07:00","id":1541602,"title":"","content":"Or be shared by Invictus Houses to keep the reign of power to a small circle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}